From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pinna <pinna@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: mediatek: accept default bias on PUPD R1/R0 pins

Amazon's Cannoli device tree uses bare bias-pull-up and bias-pull-down on
NAND and I2C pins. Generic DT parsing encodes these as MTK_ENABLE, but the
6.12 PUPD R1/R0 setter accepts only the explicit 100-103 values. The NAND
probe therefore aborts while applying pinctrl group 24, and UBI finds no
MTD on the Echo Dot (5th gen).

Restore Amazon 5.4's mapping of MTK_ENABLE to R1/R0 01. This is the default
pull used by the working stock kernel on the same satellite.
---
 drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-common-v2.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-common-v2.c b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-common-v2.c
index 3a2d6437b4f6..d3f0e1a2c456 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-common-v2.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mtk-common-v2.c
@@ -673,6 +673,9 @@ static int mtk_pinconf_bias_set_pupd_r1_r0(struct mtk_pinctrl *hw,
 	} else if (arg == MTK_PUPD_SET_R1R0_11) {
 		r0 = 1;
 		r1 = 1;
+	} else if (arg == MTK_ENABLE) {
+		r0 = 1;
+		r1 = 0;
 	} else {
 		err = -EINVAL;
 		goto out;
-- 
